commands-fr.dict is a compact derivative of the CMU Sphinx French dictionary:
https://sourceforge.net/projects/cmusphinx/files/Acoustic%20and%20Language%20Models/French/fr.dict
Source SHA-256: 40b31d1b22c4e93eb35a742dc5bf0cd4243c5966f3f306b600016a43ff55e5ec

Only the words used by Pynab's French command grammar are retained. One
pronunciation per word is selected, with the established native recognizer
preferences for est, moi, ton and météo, and the pronounced schwa variant for que.

The following missing words have manually supplied pronunciations using the
same French acoustic-model phone inventory: guili, nabaztag and tai. These
additions allow the command grammar to compile; they do not establish acoustic
accuracy for every speaker. Existing installed pronunciations take precedence.

The original dictionary's license follows in full.

